Fix BuffGetAnyLineDataW dropping everything after the first wide character

BuffGetAnyLineDataW() walks a line cell by cell, advancing `b` only on the
non-padding path. When it meets the padding cell that follows a full-width
(CJK) character it does `continue` WITHOUT advancing `b`, so `b` stays parked
on that padding cell. Every remaining iteration then sees padding too, and the
rest of the line is silently dropped.

The only caller is filesys_log.cpp:443, so the user-visible effect is that
session logging truncates any line at its first full-width character. For a
terminal with Tera Term's CJK focus that is a real data-loss bug.

Reproduction, via the qtterm oracle (which runs vtterm.c + buffer.c headless):

    printf 'ASCII \344\275\240\345\245\275 world' | oracle --cols 30 --rows 2

    before:  |ASCII 你                      |
    after:   |ASCII 你好 world              |

Found while building a differential-test harness against Tera Term 5.7.0-dev
(commit 827a35b05). Not yet reported upstream -- see oracle/README.md.

--- a/teraterm/teraterm/buffer.c
+++ b/teraterm/teraterm/buffer.c
@@ -5829,6 +5829,7 @@ int BuffGetAnyLineDataW(int offset_y, wchar_t *buf, size_t bufsize)
 	for (i = 0; i<copysize; i++) {
 		BOOL too_small;
 		size_t len;
 		if (IsBuffPadding(b)) {
+			b++;
 			continue;
 		}
 		len = expand_wchar(b, &buf[idx], left, &too_small);
